# Installer and systemd unit

- Windows is for development only. The daemon warns at startup that data-directory ACLs are unchecked on Windows.
- `scripts/install.sh` (bash, run as root with the path to a built binary) installs Golem Deploy on Ubuntu/Debian: checks (root, OS, systemd, docker CLI + daemon + `docker` group, ELF binary that runs `version`, options) all run before any change; then apt packages, the `golem-deploy` system user (in the `docker` group), `/var/lib/golem-deploy` (0700), `/usr/local/bin/golem-deploy`, `/etc/golem-deploy/golem-deploy.env` (0640 `root:golem-deploy`), optional TLS copies in `/etc/golem-deploy/tls/`, and `deploy/golem-deploy.service` (read relative to the script). It never installs Docker or touches firewall rules. Release downloads, Docker installation and setup links are later milestones.
- Idempotent: a re-run replaces binary, unit and TLS copies and restarts the service; it never rewrites an existing env file or touches an existing data directory (it refuses one with the wrong owner or mode). Keep it that way.
- A fresh install with neither listen override nor TLS files uses 443 plus an HTTP listener on 80 when both are free. Warn about busy ports and fall back to loopback. The unit grants only `CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE` so the daemon can bind low ports.
- The env file holds only `GOLEM_DEPLOY_*` variables of `serve` (`cmd/golem-deploy/main.go`). When a serve flag, its default, the data directory rules (`internal/datadir`), the plaintext/loopback rule or the port-range rules change, update the script's validation, its printed next steps and `docs/INSTALL.md`.
- The printed admin command must match `admin create` (password prompt or `--password-stdin`, explicit `--data-dir`) and run as the service user.
- The unit's hardening must stay compatible with what the daemon does: run `git`, `git-lfs`, `ssh`, the docker CLI (including `docker build` through the buildx plugin, whose build client config and state are under `<data-dir>/docker-build` and scratch files in the private `/tmp`; the build runs in dockerd) and itself (askpass); connect to `/var/run/docker.sock`; bind TCP/UDP to probe game ports; write only below the data directory (plus the non-build `DOCKER_CONFIG` in the cache directory); pass env files to docker as an inherited pipe (`/dev/fd/3`). Every directive has a comment saying why; drop a directive rather than leave it unexplained. Paths handed to dockerd (bind sources) must be the real host paths, so no `TemporaryFileSystem=`/`BindPaths=` over the data directory and no `/tmp` paths. Game containers live in dockerd's cgroup: stopping the unit must never stop them, and `TimeoutStopSec` must cover the daemon's 20-second drain and store close (`internal/httpapi/server.go`, `internal/daemon/daemon.go`).
- Verification: `shellcheck scripts/install.sh` (CI job "Shell"); `systemd-analyze verify` on the unit; run the installer in a systemd-booted Debian/Ubuntu container with the host Docker socket proxied in as `/run/docker.sock` (group `docker`), including a re-run and the failure checks; remove test containers and images afterwards.
